<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Discipline Priests</span></h2>Most crafted items aren't restricted by profession anymore, so even if you aren't a Tailor, you can still wear the Tailoring crafted items. There are a few exceptions to this, but we'll mention them below.<br/>
<br/>Most crafted items don't require you to have the profession anymore. We can wear Tailoring items, for example, even if we aren't Tailors. Note that there are some exceptions to this which we'll note below.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="phase-3-crafted-items-expensive-high-level">Phase 3 Crafted Items (Expensive, high level)</h4>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94280/falling-blossom-hood">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Hood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cloth_raidpriest_m_01helm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Hood</span></a> (requires materials from Throne of Thunder)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94279/falling-blossom-sandals">
<img alt="Falling Blossom Sandals" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cloth_raidpriest_m_01boot.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Falling Blossom Sandals</span></a> (requires materials from Throne of Thunder)</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="phase-1-2-crafted-items-cheaper-lower-level">Phase 1/<wbr/>2 Crafted Items (Cheaper, lower level)</h4>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82439/robes-of-creation">
<img alt="Robes of Creation" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_cloth_panda_b_01_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Robes of Creation</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82440/gloves-of-creation">
<img alt="Gloves of Creation" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_cloth_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gloves of Creation</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86312/legacy-of-the-emperor">
<img alt="Legacy of the Emperor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_cloth_challengepriest_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legacy of the Emperor</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86314/touch-of-the-light">
<img alt="Touch of the Light" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_cloth_challengepriest_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Touch of the Light</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77533/lightweight-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Lightweight Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Retinal Armor</span></a> (Engineering only)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> (Alchemy only). A strong pre-raid trinket that you can craft before you even hit max level!</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Discipline Priest Trinkets</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>You don't have to worry too much about whether a trinket is passive or active, since the active ones are only available at a lower item level.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94509/soothing-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Soothing Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_elemental_primal_life.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soothing Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> - A stand-out entry-level trinket.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> - An extremely strong starter trinket that you'll use for 40 or more levels. Worth the expense.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95817/lightning-imbued-chalice">
<img alt="Lightning-Imbued Chalice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_runeofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning-Imbued Chalice</span></a> - One big healing proc per minute isn't our favorite, but a large helping of intellect keeps this trinket near the top.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95641/horridons-last-gasp">
<img alt="Horridon's Last Gasp" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_eyeofthestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Horridon's Last Gasp</span></a> - A very solid mana regeneration trinket.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95712/inscribed-bag-of-hydra-spawn">
<img alt="Inscribed Bag of Hydra-Spawn" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_creature_poison_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Bag of Hydra-Spawn</span></a> - Passive spirit is miserable compared to its intellect alternatives and the proc doesn't make up for it.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95763/stolen-relic-of-zuldazar">
<img alt="Stolen Relic of Zuldazar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_twilightfireward.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stolen Relic of Zuldazar</span></a> - We already have several tools in this niche and the lack of passive intellect is expensive.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Discipline Priests</span></h2>Our <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=122098/divine-fury">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_sealofwrath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Fury</span></a> passive gives us a 100% hit chance, which means you don't need to worry about getting Hit or Expertise.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Discipline Priests</span></h2>In Phase 1 we usually gemmed to maximize socket bonuses and intellect as priority. As the expansion goes on, pure secondary gems will rise in value relative to intellect gems since we get a lot more intellect and spell power on our gear. In Phase 3, characters that are early in the gearing process can continue the intellect-focused gem strategy but geared characters (520+ ilvl) can start swapping to pure secondary gems. <b>The difference between these two gem sets isn't very big.</b>
<br/>
<br/>Blue Sockets are by far our weakest, but most socket bonuses in Phase 3 are extremely good so you're usually going to include Purple or Green gems anyway.<br/>
<br/>
